{
"ID": "e10t3",
"NAME": "March Sales per Product, Unsold Products Included",
"LANG": "sql",
"PARAMS": [],
"ENTRY": null,
"ORDERED": true,
"DESC": "<p>The merchandising team wants a sales report for March 2024 that lists every product of the catalog, including the products that sold nothing, so that they can spot dead stock.</p>\n<h3>Tables</h3>\n<p><code>products</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>product_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>primary key</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>product_name</td>\n<td>VARCHAR(50)</td>\n<td>not null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>category</td>\n<td>VARCHAR(30)</td>\n<td>may be NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>discontinued_on</td>\n<td>DATE</td>\n<td>NULL if the product is still sold</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>orders</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>order_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>primary key</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>order_date</td>\n<td>DATE</td>\n<td>not null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>status</td>\n<td>VARCHAR(20)</td>\n<td><code>'completed'</code>, <code>'pending'</code>, <code>'cancelled'</code> or <code>'refunded'</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>order_items</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>order_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>not null, exists in <code>orders</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>product_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>not null, exists in <code>products</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>quantity</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>not null, strictly positive</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>unit_price</td>\n<td>DECIMAL(10,2)</td>\n<td>not null</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>An order can contain several lines for the same product.</p>\n<h3>Rules</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>The report contains every product, except the products discontinued before <code>2024-03-01</code> (<code>discontinued_on &lt; '2024-03-01'</code>). A product with a NULL <code>discontinued_on</code>, or discontinued on or after <code>2024-03-01</code>, is included.</li>\n<li>An order line counts only if its order has status <code>'completed'</code> and an <code>order_date</code> between <code>2024-03-01</code> and <code>2024-03-31</code>, both inclusive.</li>\n<li><code>orders_count</code> is the number of distinct counted orders that contain the product, <code>units_sold</code> is the sum of <code>quantity</code>, and <code>revenue</code> is the sum of <code>quantity * unit_price</code> over the counted lines. A product without any counted line has <code>0</code>, <code>0</code> and <code>0.00</code>.</li>\n<li>A NULL <code>category</code> is reported as <code>'Uncategorized'</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Output</h3>\n<p>Exactly these columns, in this order:</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>category</td>\n<td>VARCHAR</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>product_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>product_name</td>\n<td>VARCHAR</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>orders_count</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>units_sold</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>revenue</td>\n<td>DECIMAL, 2 decimals</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Rows are sorted by <code>category</code> ascending, then <code>revenue</code> descending, then <code>product_id</code> ascending.</p>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p><code>products</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>product_id</th>\n<th>product_name</th>\n<th>category</th>\n<th>discontinued_on</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Pen</td>\n<td>Office</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Notebook</td>\n<td>Office</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Stapler</td>\n<td>Office</td>\n<td>2024-02-15</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Mouse</td>\n<td>Electronics</td>\n<td>2024-03-20</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Cable</td>\n<td>Electronics</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Mug</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>orders</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>order_id</th>\n<th>order_date</th>\n<th>status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>2024-03-02</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>101</td>\n<td>2024-03-15</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>102</td>\n<td>2024-03-20</td>\n<td>cancelled</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>103</td>\n<td>2024-02-28</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>104</td>\n<td>2024-03-31</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>order_items</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>order_id</th>\n<th>product_id</th>\n<th>quantity</th>\n<th>unit_price</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>1.50</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>25.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>101</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>1.50</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>101</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>4.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>102</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>9.99</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>103</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>4.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>104</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>24.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>104</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>12.00</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Expected output</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>category</th>\n<th>product_id</th>\n<th>product_name</th>\n<th>orders_count</th>\n<th>units_sold</th>\n<th>revenue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Electronics</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Mouse</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>73.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Electronics</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Cable</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Office</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Pen</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>22.50</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Office</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Notebook</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>8.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Uncategorized</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Mug</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Constraints</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Dialect: PostgreSQL.</li>\n<li>Write a single <code>SELECT</code> statement (CTEs allowed). Do not create tables or views.</li>\n<li><code>products</code> has up to 10^5 rows, <code>orders</code> up to 10^6 rows, <code>order_items</code> up to 5 * 10^6 rows.</li>\n</ul><p class=\"muted\">Write a PostgreSQL query.</p>",
"STARTER": "/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n",
"SOLUTION": "-- Q3 : solution de référence PostgreSQL (tourne aussi telle quelle sur MySQL 8 et DuckDB)\nWITH march_sales AS (\n    -- 1. On agrège D'ABORD les ventes valides (commande completed, en mars 2024), par produit.\n    SELECT oi.product_id,\n           COUNT(DISTINCT oi.order_id)       AS orders_count,\n           SUM(oi.quantity)                  AS units_sold,\n           SUM(oi.quantity * oi.unit_price)  AS revenue\n    FROM order_items oi\n    JOIN orders o\n      ON o.order_id = oi.order_id\n    WHERE o.status = 'completed'\n      AND o.order_date >= DATE '2024-03-01'\n      AND o.order_date <  DATE '2024-04-01'\n    GROUP BY oi.product_id\n)\n-- 2. Puis LEFT JOIN depuis products : les produits sans vente gardent une ligne (valeurs NULL => 0).\nSELECT COALESCE(p.category, 'Uncategorized') AS category,\n       p.product_id,\n       p.product_name,\n       COALESCE(s.orders_count, 0) AS orders_count,\n       COALESCE(s.units_sold, 0)   AS units_sold,\n       COALESCE(s.revenue, 0)      AS revenue\nFROM products p\nLEFT JOIN march_sales s\n  ON s.product_id = p.product_id\nWHERE p.discontinued_on IS NULL\n   OR p.discontinued_on >= DATE '2024-03-01'\nORDER BY category ASC, revenue DESC, p.product_id ASC;\n",
"WRAPPER": "",
"MINUTES": 22,
"SOURCE": "Examen d'entraînement d'octobre n°2, question 3",
